The key architectural point in 2C.2 is that the indexer should never “repair” blockchain state itself. Its job is only to determine which branch Core currently considers canonical; the already-reviewed Store remains responsible for atomically applying a block or rolling back to an explicitly selected ancestor. RollbackTo was deliberately written with exactly that division of responsibility.

And keeping sync_state('main') as the single durable resume point means the new live loop does not reintroduce the kind of independent checkpoint/data state that caused the old eIquidus crash-replay corruption. Store.Tip() already exposes that durable checkpoint specifically for the future indexer.
